## Separation of Concerns & DI

- UI components handle rendering + user input only; domain/services handle business rules; storage/sync modules handle persistence and external IO.
- Use constructor injection or explicit parameter passing for dependencies; depend on interfaces/modules for external providers.
- Extract shared logic to services or helpers when:
  - Method exceeds its single responsibility
  - Logic is reused across screens/services
  - Unit testing the logic in isolation is valuable

Minimal helper guidance:
- Keep helpers pure and stateless; avoid coupling to framework globals where possible
